You can combine it with nginx that can provide a basic auth easily. The example of nginx.conf as following:

```
server {
    listen 443 ssl;

    server_name your.server.domain;

    ssl_certificate your.server.domain.crt;
    ssl_certificate_key your.server.domain.key;

    location / {
        auth_basic           "ChatGPT Next";
        auth_basic_user_file conf/htpasswd;
        proxy_pass http://backend.chatgpt;
    }    
}
```
Now, you can access to <https://your.server.domain>, but you will be demanded to provide user and password matched with credentials in `conf/htpasswd`.

More details in <https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_auth_basic_module.html>

@Jcontre905, to remove masks, in the `app/masks/index.ts` file remove `CN_MASKS` and `EN_MASKS` usage. It will be replacing

```typescript
export const BUILTIN_MASKS: Mask[] = [...CN_MASKS, ...EN_MASKS].map((m) =>
  BUILTIN_MASK_STORE.add(m),
);
```

to

```typescript
export const BUILTIN_MASKS: Mask[] = [];
```

Also you can remove files `app/masks/cn.ts` and `app\masks\en.ts`, if need to clear more files. And remove imports of these files.

If you need also disable promts, in the `app\store\prompt.ts` file you can replace 

```typescript
let fetchPrompts = [res.en, res.cn];
```

to

```typescript
let fetchPrompts: PromptList[] = [];
```

